WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:02.880
Mutants, multiversal fakeouts,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:02.880 --> 00:00:07.560
and good guys gone bad — Marvel's phase&nbsp;
4 has really kept fans on their toes.

00:00:09.408 --> 00:00:12.240
Evan Peters played Quicksilver in&nbsp;
the Fox-produced "X-Men" films,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:18.300
which prior to 2021 had been disconnected from&nbsp;
the MCU timeline. That all seemed to change,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:22.680
however, when Peters showed up on Wanda's&nbsp;
doorstep in "WandaVision." Previously,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:25.980
the MCU's Quicksilver was&nbsp;
played by Aaron Taylor-Johnson,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:30.300
and the character was killed off in the line&nbsp;
of duty during "Avengers: Age of Ultron."

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:35.340
The appearance of Peters sent Marvel fans&nbsp;
speculating wildly. The actor's appearance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:39.900
as Wanda's brother Pietro seemingly opened&nbsp;
the floodgates of the multiverse and perhaps&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:45.240
indicated that "X-Men" actors such as Patrick&nbsp;
Stewart and Hugh Jackman could also show up.

00:00:45.240 --> 00:00:49.680
So, was Peters playing the Taylor-Johnson&nbsp;
version of Quicksilver who had somehow been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:52.980
resurrected? Or was he a visitor&nbsp;
from an alternate universe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.980 --> 00:00:56.760
thus making the "X-Men" films&nbsp;
tangentially canon to the MCU?

00:00:56.760 --> 00:01:01.800
Much of this speculation would ultimately&nbsp;
be squashed, as Peters' character in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:06.300
show was revealed to be … a random&nbsp;
Westview citizen named Ralph Bohner,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:10.740
cast by Agatha Harkness to pretend to be&nbsp;
Wanda's brother. Though this MacGuffin may&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:14.760
have ultimately proven anticlimactic,&nbsp;
it yielded some wild theories,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.760 --> 00:01:18.800
and may have been a none-too-subtle&nbsp;
foreshadowing of the chaos to come.

00:01:20.332 --> 00:01:24.240
Sam and Bucky found themselves reunited with&nbsp;
Sharon Carter in "The Falcon and the Winter&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:29.220
Soldier." A criminal in the eyes of the American&nbsp;
government because she assisted Captain America&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.220 --> 00:01:34.560
during the events of "Civil War," Sharon was now&nbsp;
living in Madripoor. Meanwhile, throughout the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:39.900
series, there was constant mention of a mysterious&nbsp;
Power Broker, who sold access to super-powers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.900 --> 00:01:45.060
to anyone who could pay and ruled Madripoor's&nbsp;
underworld. The figure was heavily involved in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.060 --> 00:01:49.860
Madripoor's business and sounded like a potential&nbsp;
big bad our heroes would eventually face.

00:01:49.860 --> 00:01:53.580
But although Sharon appeared to be aiding&nbsp;
Sam and Bucky throughout the series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.580 --> 00:01:57.120
she would eventually be revealed&nbsp;
as the Power Broker herself,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.120 --> 00:02:01.260
leading to a number of follow-up&nbsp;
questions yet to be answered in the MCU.

00:02:01.260 --> 00:02:06.360
Then, in a post-credits scene for the series,&nbsp;
Carter was seemingly pardoned for aiding Captain&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.360 --> 00:02:11.880
America by the US government and reinstated&nbsp;
as an agent — but as we saw shortly afterward,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.880 --> 00:02:17.340
she's still maintaining her identity as the Power&nbsp;
Broker. The intricate web of Sharon Carter's true&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.340 --> 00:02:23.280
intentions, and what may have led to this 180&nbsp;
in allegiances, continues to hang over the MCU.

00:02:24.360 --> 00:02:26.760
"I'm trying something different.&nbsp;
Maybe you should do the same."

00:02:28.734 --> 00:02:33.720
Wenwu spent centuries as the Mandarin, performing&nbsp;
acts of terrorism within an organization known&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:39.420
as the Ten Rings, named after the ten magical&nbsp;
rings that gave him his long life. Wenwu's son,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.420 --> 00:02:44.100
Shang-Chi, came to reckon with his father's&nbsp;
exploits in adulthood. He grappled with his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.100 --> 00:02:48.060
family's history and eventually sought&nbsp;
to stop his father once and for all.

00:02:48.060 --> 00:02:52.680
During the entirety of "Shang-Chi and the&nbsp;
Legend of the Ten Rings," Wenwu was painted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.680 --> 00:02:58.020
as a criminal and a terrible father to his&nbsp;
children. However, as MCU fans saw in the film,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.020 --> 00:03:02.580
Wenwu mistakenly believed his deceased&nbsp;
wife was alive and being held captive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.580 --> 00:03:07.320
by the Dweller-In-Darkness, a creature best&nbsp;
described as a cross between a demon and a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:12.180
dragon. This delusion acted as Wenwu's&nbsp;
justification for his wrongdoings. So,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.180 --> 00:03:17.340
what did it take for Wenwu to realize that his&nbsp;
quest was a fool's errand? The answer is, his son.

00:03:17.340 --> 00:03:23.400
In turn, Wenwu awoke to his mistakes and repented,&nbsp;
sacrificing his life to the monster while also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.400 --> 00:03:28.980
giving his son control over the powerful rings.&nbsp;
It was a powerful last-minute redemption, with a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.980 --> 00:03:34.380
longtime villain turning over a new leaf, hoping&nbsp;
his final act can make up for a lifetime of pain.

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:41.280
"Dad, please… Your family needs you."

00:03:43.847 --> 00:03:47.820
Laura Barton made her MCU debut in "Avengers:&nbsp;
Age of Ultron," when the audience learned that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.820 --> 00:03:52.680
Hawkeye had a wife and kids he'd been keeping a&nbsp;
secret while performing his superheroic duties.

00:03:52.680 --> 00:03:57.300
In "Ultron" and some other minor appearances,&nbsp;
there was little to suggest the character was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.300 --> 00:04:01.560
anything more than your average, ordinary,&nbsp;
run-of-the-mill superhero spouse. That is,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.560 --> 00:04:05.880
until the Disney+ series "Hawkeye," in&nbsp;
which Laura suddenly seemed very invested&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.880 --> 00:04:10.080
in a Rolex watch that Hawkeye was trying&nbsp;
to track down. We were told the watch had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.080 --> 00:04:14.460
connections to its former owner's identity,&nbsp;
which could be compromised if the watch fell&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.460 --> 00:04:18.780
into the wrong hands. Hawkeye succeeded&nbsp;
in procuring the watch, whose owner was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.780 --> 00:04:22.860
revealed to be Laura herself. And the capper&nbsp;
is that she's a former agent of S.H.I.E.L.D.

00:04:22.860 --> 00:04:27.480
This plot twist presents a fun dynamic with&nbsp;
which to revisit Laura's appearances up to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.480 --> 00:04:31.380
this point. In hindsight, the character was&nbsp;
keeping a huge part of herself a secret.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.380 --> 00:04:36.840
Looking ahead to the future, it presents exciting&nbsp;
opportunities to hopefully see her in action.

00:04:38.160 --> 00:04:39.025
"Thank you."

00:04:39.060 --> 00:04:45.840
From 2015 to 2019, Marvel Television created&nbsp;
several shows for Netflix that referenced events&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:52.080
within the MCU, yet were seemingly unrelated to&nbsp;
Marvel Studios. When Disney+ launched in 2019,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.080 --> 00:04:56.160
as Marvel Studios announced a slate of&nbsp;
shows for the new streaming platform,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.160 --> 00:05:01.020
the Netflix partnership was terminated and&nbsp;
those stories and characters seemed likely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.020 --> 00:05:05.880
to be narratively dismissed going forward.&nbsp;
Even so, fans expressed their desire to see&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:05.880 --> 00:05:10.380
the continuation of these versions of&nbsp;
Daredevil, Jessica Jones, and others.

00:05:10.380 --> 00:05:16.440
After a long period of radio silence, hope&nbsp;
emerged in December 2021, which saw the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.440 --> 00:05:21.420
sudden return of two beloved portrayals in a&nbsp;
big way. First Kingpin appeared as a villain&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.420 --> 00:05:27.000
in "Hawkeye," with Vincent D'Onofrio reprising his&nbsp;
role from the "Daredevil" series. That same month,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:31.260
Charlie Cox made a surprise appearance as&nbsp;
Matt Murdock in "Spider-Man: No Way Home."

00:05:31.260 --> 00:05:36.180
Even after Daredevil's subsequent appearance&nbsp;
on "She-Hulk," details are still fuzzy as to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.180 --> 00:05:40.320
whether these are the same versions of those&nbsp;
characters from their Netflix incarnations,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.320 --> 00:05:44.820
or if what fans are seeing is in some&nbsp;
sort of alternate timeline. Nevertheless,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.820 --> 00:05:48.960
these are huge Marvel characters, so&nbsp;
clearly they are a necessary piece&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.960 --> 00:05:53.400
of the puzzle and it's good to see the MCU&nbsp;
won't be rolling the dice with recastings.

00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:57.840
While the biggest reveal of "Spider-Man:&nbsp;
No Way Home" was undoubtedly the return&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:57.840 --> 00:06:02.400
of Tobey Maguire and Andrew Garfield as&nbsp;
their respective versions of Peter Parker,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.400 --> 00:06:06.840
the film had even more tricks up its sleeve.&nbsp;
One could argue that the film's conclusion&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:06.840 --> 00:06:10.800
of Doctor Strange wiping the world's&nbsp;
memories of Peter Parker will hold far&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:10.800 --> 00:06:15.360
longer-lasting repercussions in future MCU&nbsp;
installments than most people could imagine.

00:06:15.360 --> 00:06:19.440
Thanks to a Strange spell gone wrong,&nbsp;
individuals from countless universes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:19.440 --> 00:06:23.640
aware that Peter Parker is Spider-Man&nbsp;
were in the process of being transported&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:23.640 --> 00:06:27.720
to the MCU's primary timeline. While&nbsp;
that spell could not be reversed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:27.720 --> 00:06:31.200
its outcome could be changed and save&nbsp;
Peter and his friends from danger.

00:06:31.200 --> 00:06:36.300
To save the timeline from imploding, Peter&nbsp;
and Strange devised a desperate plan to rid&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:36.300 --> 00:06:41.400
the world's memory of Peter Parker, leaving&nbsp;
the young hero completely alone in the proces.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:41.400 --> 00:06:47.040
It was a juggernaut of an ending for an already&nbsp;
emotional story, with the touching nature of its&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:47.040 --> 00:06:51.600
final scenes bringing a tragically beautiful&nbsp;
conclusion to this "Spider-Man" trilogy.

00:06:56.220 --> 00:07:00.600
Early trailers for "Doctor Strange in the&nbsp;
Multiverse of Madness" seemed to tease a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:00.600 --> 00:07:04.980
team-up of sorts, with Marvel's Sorcerer&nbsp;
Supreme and its Scarlet Witch embarking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:04.980 --> 00:07:09.000
on a mission together. The ads also made&nbsp;
it seem like the film's plot would revolve&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:09.000 --> 00:07:13.140
around the fallout from Doctor Strange's&nbsp;
multiverse-tampering actions in "Spider-Man:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:13.140 --> 00:07:18.300
No Way Home." As it turns out, both were&nbsp;
misdirections to throw us off the real story here.

00:07:18.300 --> 00:07:23.040
MCU fans were shocked when Doctor Strange&nbsp;
discovered Wanda was in control of the very&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:23.040 --> 00:07:27.720
monsters he'd sought out her support to help&nbsp;
him fight. Determined to gain access to another&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:27.720 --> 00:07:32.460
reality in which she could be a mother to her twin&nbsp;
boys from "WandaVision," the Scarlet Witch would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:32.460 --> 00:07:37.260
stop at nothing to achieve her heart's desire.&nbsp;
With an incredible performance by Elizabeth Olsen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:37.260 --> 00:07:42.000
Wanda in "Multiverse of Madness" was a&nbsp;
surprisingly wicked and powerful antagonist.

00:07:42.660 --> 00:07:47.100
Trailers for "Doctor Strange in the Multiverse&nbsp;
of Madness" hinted at the film's inclusion of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:47.100 --> 00:07:51.120
heroes from across the multiverse, and they&nbsp;
appeared in the form of the Illuminati,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:51.120 --> 00:07:56.160
a supergroup of Marvel characters. As teased with&nbsp;
an audio clip in one of the movie's trailers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:56.160 --> 00:08:00.120
Patrick Stewart's version of Professor&nbsp;
Charles Xavier — seemingly from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:00.120 --> 00:08:05.340
Fox-made "X-Men" films — was among them.&nbsp;
But he was hardly alone — as it turned out,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:05.340 --> 00:08:10.560
this Xavier was but one member of an alternate&nbsp;
reality super-team known as the Illuminati.

00:08:10.560 --> 00:08:16.980
In addition to Professor X, the roster included&nbsp;
Karl Mordo, Captain Peggy Carter, Maria Rambeau,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:16.980 --> 00:08:22.740
Black Bolt, and Reed Richards. Nearly every&nbsp;
character was played by veteran Marvel actors&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:22.740 --> 00:08:27.000
returning to play variant versions of&nbsp;
their previous roles. But Mr. Fantastic,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:27.000 --> 00:08:32.100
as portrayed by John Krasinksi, was&nbsp;
fancasting come true, as Marvel Studios&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:32.100 --> 00:08:36.960
President Kevin Feige was happy to indulge&nbsp;
months of fans urging Krasinski's casting.

00:08:36.960 --> 00:08:41.580
While the jury is still out on whether Mr.&nbsp;
Fantastic will look like Krasinksi in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:41.580 --> 00:08:46.680
upcoming "Fantastic Four" film, Reed's brief&nbsp;
moment alongside the rest of the other eclectic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:46.680 --> 00:08:50.940
members of the Illuminati was a thrilling&nbsp;
tribute to Marvel media over the years.

00:08:51.780 --> 00:08:56.100
In the first season of "Loki," the titular&nbsp;
character found himself at the headquarters of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:56.100 --> 00:09:00.780
the Time Variance Authority. The organization's&nbsp;
mission was seemingly to control the entire&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:00.780 --> 00:09:05.700
timeline of the universe and stamp out any&nbsp;
"variants" which may occur. Going by the motto&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:05.700 --> 00:09:10.980
"for all time, always," the TVA's no-nonsense,&nbsp;
bureaucratic ways were hellbent on maintaining&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:10.980 --> 00:09:15.840
the so-called "Sacred Timeline." Through a series&nbsp;
of convoluted explanations and revelations,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:15.840 --> 00:09:21.060
MCU fans learned that the TVA was seemingly&nbsp;
responsible for maintaining the integrity of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:21.060 --> 00:09:26.400
existence itself with mysterious figures known as&nbsp;
the Time-Keepers overseeing the whole operation.

00:09:26.400 --> 00:09:29.820
The audience would ultimately have the&nbsp;
rug pulled out from under them, however,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:29.820 --> 00:09:35.520
when Loki and Sylvie discovered that the TVA&nbsp;
was merely a false front. The TVA's agents were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:35.520 --> 00:09:40.080
unaware that the Time-Keepers were robots, and the&nbsp;
agents had past lives they'd been made to forget.

00:09:40.080 --> 00:09:45.780
The TVA, and its stated purpose of controlling the&nbsp;
Sacred Timeline, was an elaborate lie hiding the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:45.780 --> 00:09:50.340
actions committed by He Who Remains. Better&nbsp;
known to Marvel fans as Kang the Conqueror,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:50.340 --> 00:09:55.140
he disrupted time when multiple versions of&nbsp;
himself from other timelines tried to interfere&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:55.140 --> 00:10:00.900
long ago — and he created the TVA to make his&nbsp;
timeline the only timeline. There is more Kang&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:00.900 --> 00:10:06.060
to come in future MCU projects, but his initial&nbsp;
reveal was a plot-twist disruption from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:06.060 --> 00:10:11.100
aforementioned logic of "Loki," perhaps laying&nbsp;
the groundwork for future misdeeds yet to come.

00:10:12.060 --> 00:10:15.960
The titular heroes of "Eternals" had a&nbsp;
long held belief that they existed to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:15.960 --> 00:10:19.800
keep Earth safe. As it turned out, they&nbsp;
were actually just conduits to prepare&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:19.800 --> 00:10:24.120
Earth's inhabitants for extinction upon&nbsp;
the birth of a being known as a Celestial.

00:10:24.120 --> 00:10:28.260
As MCU fans discovered alongside the&nbsp;
film's characters, they've already done&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:28.260 --> 00:10:32.280
this countless times with other planets,&nbsp;
but they just can't remember. What to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:32.280 --> 00:10:36.300
viewer was a mere plot twist was, to the&nbsp;
characters, the disruption of their entire&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:36.300 --> 00:10:40.200
reason for existing and their overall&nbsp;
perception of the world's existence.

00:10:40.200 --> 00:10:44.640
Now that they know the truth, the Eternals&nbsp;
go forward unwilling to continue as pawns&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:44.640 --> 00:10:48.600
in a scheme for the mass extermination&nbsp;
of all life forms on Earth. Instead,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:48.600 --> 00:10:52.200
they are determined to challenge what's&nbsp;
expected of them and save the planet in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:52.200 --> 00:10:56.040
doing so. Like "Loki," the world-building&nbsp;
of "Eternals" was quite complicated,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:56.040 --> 00:11:00.780
and the repercussions of its big "gotcha"&nbsp;
moment have yet to be fully understood.

00:11:01.980 --> 00:11:06.480
With Phase 4's inclusion in the MCU's&nbsp;
"Multiverse Saga," opportunities have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:06.480 --> 00:11:11.220
begun presenting themselves for the occasional&nbsp;
cross-pollination of franchises. Chief among&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:11.220 --> 00:11:15.660
these seems to be "X-Men" alumni, as Evan&nbsp;
Peters and Patrick Stewart were both members&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:15.660 --> 00:11:20.940
of the beloved Fox "X-Men" movies and now have&nbsp;
at least some tangential place in the MCU.

00:11:20.940 --> 00:11:25.380
However, Marvel Studios has yet to&nbsp;
formally establish the X-Men as a part&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:25.380 --> 00:11:29.760
of the MCU proper. Therefore, a detail&nbsp;
at the end of the "Ms. Marvel" series&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:29.760 --> 00:11:33.900
came as a huge reveal, perhaps setting&nbsp;
up significant repercussions to come.

00:11:33.900 --> 00:11:39.180
Early in the series, Kamala Khan inherited&nbsp;
a powerful bangle from her grandmother and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:39.180 --> 00:11:43.320
immediately gained superpowers, making it&nbsp;
seem as though the power was derived from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:43.320 --> 00:11:47.280
the bangle itself. But with help from the&nbsp;
scientific findings of her friend Bruno,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:47.280 --> 00:11:50.640
Kamala would come to learn that&nbsp;
the powers were within her genetic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:50.640 --> 00:11:54.720
structure all along. The bangle simply&nbsp;
unlocked what had already been present.

00:11:54.720 --> 00:11:59.220
In the last episode's final moments,&nbsp;
Bruno shared another layer of discovery,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:59.220 --> 00:12:03.060
explaining she possessed a mutation&nbsp;
while a music cue from "X-Men:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:03.060 --> 00:12:05.040
The Animated Series" played in the background.

00:12:06.120 --> 00:12:13.200
"There's something different in&nbsp;
your genes, like a mutation."

00:12:15.960 --> 00:12:20.220
This was big news in an MCU that had never&nbsp;
said the word "mutant" before for various&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:20.220 --> 00:12:24.780
reasons, and was now seemingly laying the&nbsp;
foundation for the X-Men for the first time.

00:12:24.780 --> 00:12:29.220
Kamala shrugged off the news, simply&nbsp;
referring to it as a label. But could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:29.220 --> 00:12:32.880
the revelation possibly open the door for&nbsp;
"X-Men" to be more prominently featured&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:32.880 --> 00:12:37.980
in the MCU going forward? As Stan Lee&nbsp;
might say, stay tuned, true believers.

